	(text "The board is fed from the ESC BEC and never from raw VBAT:\nmotor braking spikes on a 6S pack can exceed the 32 V input\nrating of the AP63205, and the BEC absorbs them. Measured\nsource: T-Motor Velox 45A V2, 10 V BEC."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 114.3 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "0b9463df-942d-4bbe-bc73-30f13590c96d")
	)
	(text "The divider now hangs on the raw battery instead of a\nregulated rail, so pack voltage is directly visible; the old\ninput-rail divider could not see it.\nR1/R2 = 100k/12k, ratio 12/112 = 0.10714.\nTap = 2.70 V at 25.2 V (6S max), 1.80 V at 16.8 V (4S max),\nand 3.3 V (VDDA) is reached only at 30.8 V, so any plausible\npack transient stays inside the ADC range.\nDrain 0.22 mA continuous while the pack is plugged; source\nimpedance 10.7 k, fine because C7 sits at the pin and the\nconversion runs at about 1 Hz with a long sampling time.\nD3 clamps negative excursions: DS11853 Table 60 allows\nzero negative current injection on PC0..PC3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 127 147.066 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "38dbbbd4-fa8c-455a-9ea3-827fba663572")
	)
	(text "3V3 LDO (PWR-2)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 160.02 53.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "70879541-182d-46f2-80e6-0f9ce9f97e09")
	)
	(text "VBAT sense to ADC, raw battery at the ESC pad group (PWR-4)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 118.11 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "7f6a3e4d-7dc8-41d2-80aa-fc9888aa8816")
	)
	(text "5 V active OR-ing / power mux (PWR-3)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 199.39 53.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a5000000-1000-4000-8000-000000000014")
	)
	(text "U8 replaces the two Schottky ORing diodes: 40 mOhm typical (60 mOhm over\ntemperature) instead of 300 mV of drop, and it blocks in BOTH legs, so USB\n5 V cannot back-drive the AP63205 output through its high-side body diode.\nMODE tied to VIN1 selects priority mode: the BEC wins whenever it is there,\nso plugging or unplugging USB never disturbs a board that is already flying.\nR18/R19 set the switchover threshold at VREF * 133/33 = 4.03 V on VIN1\n(VREF = 0.92 to 1.08 V, so 3.7 to 4.35 V worst case; the buck holds 5 V\n+/-2 %, so no parasitic switchover).\nWith VIN1 dead (bench, USB only) MODE is low and PR1 is low, and the truth\ntable passes the higher of the two inputs: the board runs on USB with\nnothing to command.\nSwitchover is BREAK-before-make, tSW = 8 us at 5 V: C5 + C26 keep the droop\nnear 145 mV at 400 mA.\nVIN abs max is 6 V (5.5 V recommended). Unlike the Schottky stage, this node\nis no longer indifferent to a USB overvoltage. No extra TVS was added for\nthat (2026-08-17): U7 (USBLC6-2SC6) already clamps VBUS at VBR 6.1 V, and no\npassive part can hold 5.25 V and cap at 6 V - only an active OVP switch could,\nand a compliant UFP source never leaves 5 V. See PWR-3."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 199.39 142.24 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "a5000000-1000-4000-8000-000000000015")
	)
	(text "U1 is the fixed 5 V version: FB is tied to the buck output (5V_BUCK)\nper the datasheet, and EN is tied to VIN (always on).\nOR stage: D1 also blocks the AP63205 high-side body diode, so USB\npower on the shared rail cannot back-feed the 10 V net (PWR-3)."
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 105.41 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.27 1.27)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "beadd1b7-c763-4f87-b32a-3a41959924c1")
	)
	(text "10 V BEC input and 5 V buck (PWR-1)"
		(exclude_from_sim no)
		(at 40.64 53.34 0)
		(effects
			(font
				(size 1.778 1.778)
				(bold yes)
			)
			(justify left bottom)
		)
		(uuid "f5ad0481-bc5c-45e7-a0a1-200a9891c33e")
	)
